{"entryId":"1123","paragraphs":[{"sourceId":"heilprin:sefaria-warsaw:ta:1123:1","sourceSha256":"a68156740be1afb9d2a37cf57428b0f81f10a3395242910db0b8e521a4b08651","englishSha256":"2e94f1d1652b9c37f7bd63d1f0395b74987003c35e62be816de8bfbfdca76522","citations":[{"id":"1123:1:cite-01","he":[27,45],"en":[53,83],"target":{"entry":1766,"paragraph":1},"reference":"Seder HaDorot, Tanaim and Amoraim 1766:1","assessment":"Multiple texts attest the patronymic and relative. The next line in Shabbat specifically offers Yehoshua ben Kefosai, son-in-law of Akiva, as the alternate participant in that scene. This differs from the proof in Chullin and its Demai parallel.","evidence":[{"reference":"Shabbat 147a:9","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Shabbat_147a.9"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Shabbat 147a:10","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Shabbat_147a.10"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Chullin 6b:5","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Chullin_6b.5"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Jerusalem Talmud Demai 2:1:11","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Jerusalem_Talmud_Demai_2.1.11"},"witness":"The Jerusalem Talmud, edition by Heinrich W. Guggenheimer. Berlin, De Gruyter, 1999-2015"},{"reference":"Seder HaDorot 1766:1","target":{"entry":1766,"paragraph":1},"witness":"Pinned Warsaw digital witness"}]}],"inlineHebrew":[0],"holds":[{"raw":"זירוז או זירון","reason":"Witnesses and internal entries vary in spelling. The next Shabbat line proposes an alternate participant in its scene.","evidence":[{"reference":"Shabbat 147a:9","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Shabbat_147a.9"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Shabbat 147a:10","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Shabbat_147a.10"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Chullin 6b:5","target":{"url":"https://www.sefari